  Cell[
   "Inserts and symmetrizes the little-group indices of one massive \
particle.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"SymmetrizeSpin", "[", "expr", ",",
         " ", "i", ",", " ", "{", "indices", "}", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     "  ", "averages the distinct index permutations for particle i."}],
   "Usage"], Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The routine acts on the \
implicit massive spinor factors of the specified particle. It supports one \
through four indices.", "Notes"], Cell["The average is over distinct \
permutations, so coincident index labels retain their proper normalization. \
This is little-group symmetrization, not a permutation of identical external \
particles.", "Notes"],
  Cell[
   "Use ChooseSpinIndex to select a normalized physical spin projection.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
